//   Just as for AMOs in the a extension, ssamoswap.w or ssamoswap.d requires that the address held
//     in rs1 be naturally aligned to the size of the operand (i.e., 8-byte aligned for doublewords,
//     and 4-byte aligned for words). The same exception options apply if the address is not
//     naturally aligned.
//
// Context:
//   A misaligned AMO raises a store/AMO address-misaligned (6) or store/AMO access-fault (7)
//     exception, xtval 0 or the address. The misaligned atomicity granule does not apply to
//     ssamoswap (#3425, PR #3426), so even an address inside a 16-byte granule must trap.
//
